  "scope_limits": {
    "installed_source": "Original configured Observation.rawRestriction comes from Assembly.rawInstallation through existing inherited optional/query/result/consumer/compilation faces and actual source visit. stockRawRestriction copies its projection, active, classifier_eq and payload_eq; no projection, equality certificate or target payload is supplied by a caller.",
    "stock_root": "Existing StockObservation.root uses Observation.Material.root, which changes observationAt only and preserves original source projection law, emitted occurrence, compiler_commutes and ledger. Existing same_ledger is rfl. CP115 adds no new law, embedding, coface, root or no-next gate.",
    "actual_next": "rawAtNext transports that actual restriction by signed113 actual_born_root_current generated from original actual_segment, source successor_valid and its own stopping receipt. It is indexed by the literal canonical next root/current and emitted occurrence; cofinalRaw retains original D.index recurrence and native Lower W grade.",
    "request_identity": "stock_raw_read/raw_registered recover original registered UniformRaw. installed_request proves both installed read.environment and installed read.expression equal the signed113 typed actual request fields. UniformRaw is an Env/expression readout; the source owner remains in the signed113 typed request/material and is not a newly invented projection field.",
    "direct_laws": "installed_effect, installed_inverse, installed_zero_iff and installed_affine use installed_request in their value/proof bodies and consume original signed113 cofinal registered laws. Their left/right mouths actually contain O.readRaw of cofinalRaw, not a detached registered expression.",
    "environment_sigma": "Registered execution Env, decoded born.activeEnvironment, previous completed native sigma and fresh local residual retain distinct indices. Decoded Env only supplies the original source delta evaluation of previous sigma. No depth0 or historical relation-membership zero is inferred.",
